00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,000
Trace parts.
Export CAD. Free, open-source tracing software for makers. A mounting plate, traced, measured and ready to export.

2
00:00:05,000 --> 00:00:10,000
A part with no CAD file. My dad and I needed to recreate it. Photo tracing was frustrating. Alternatives were expensive.

3
00:00:10,000 --> 00:00:24,000
Import a reference image and trace the outer profile.

4
00:00:24,000 --> 00:00:33,000
Choose Circle → 3-Pt. Pick three points around the hole.

5
00:00:33,000 --> 00:00:46,000
Trace the remaining holes and slot; review each fitted shape.

6
00:00:46,000 --> 00:00:49,000
Review the complete profile, rounded corners and openings.

7
00:00:49,000 --> 00:00:58,000
Use a known dimension: this sample is 80 mm tall.

8
00:00:58,000 --> 00:01:04,000
Export the finished part as DXF, SVG or PDF.

9
00:01:04,000 --> 00:01:09,000
Or take a photo from above and import it.

10
00:01:09,000 --> 00:01:18,000
Generate an outline. Review it and set scale before export.

11
00:01:18,000 --> 00:01:24,000
Built for your workflow. JavaScript · HTML · CSS · Canvas · Electron Optional auto-outline: pretrained MobileSAM + ONNX Runtime.

12
00:01:24,000 --> 00:01:32,000
Tracing functionality by Nik Horner. CAD curve fitting · hands-on testing · ML direction AI coding tools: Codex and Claude Code. AI also assisted this video.

13
00:01:32,000 --> 00:01:35,000
TrueLine github.com/Nik-Horner/TrueLine Trace. Review. Scale. Export.
